Subject: [PATCH 4/5] docs(governance): correct ADR-105 governance record after
 real 6-seat panel

A real, independent 6-agent adr-review panel (architect, critic, security,
independent-thinker, analyst, high-level-advisor, each a separate agent
invocation, no shared context) replaces the invalid prior debate log, which
admitted it was produced by a single orchestrated session simulating all
six seats. Two independent PR reviewers (Copilot, CodeRabbit) correctly
rejected that prior artifact per adr-review/SKILL.md's own anti-pattern
table.

Round 1 result: 5 Block, 1 Disagree-and-Commit. Convergent findings across
seats: the debate-log fabrication itself; ADR-105's none-duplicating claim
is false (the terminal predicate is restated in 3 files); the
mandatory-policy-over-user-request carve-out (fixed once in the skill and
builder-ethos.md section 3) was still missing from builder-ethos.md's
Precedence Stack item 1, Decision Procedure step 1, and voice.md's tier-3
User overrides entry (the last of which also self-contradicted its own
tier-1 dash-ban claim). A separate implementer round (already committed:
eae055405, 6357a2664) fixed the precedence-qualifier gap and 4 other
findings; this commit updates the ADR text and Consensus section, and the
debate log, to match.

status reverted to proposed: Round 2 (re-collecting the same 6 seats
verdict against the post-fix diff) was not run in this session, disclosed
here rather than silently claimed. A future session must run Round 2
before this ADR may transition to accepted, per ADR-073.

Regenerated .agents/architecture/README.md via generate_adr_index.py.
